  <Metadata Name="D1 56578: voice-port wrapper null guards (synthetic)"
            isEnabled="true" AppVer="01.00" AppElf="eboot.bin" Author="d1reimagined" PatchVer="1.0">
    <!-- 0xB47E50 is `mov edi,[rdi+8]; movzx esi,sil; jmp sceVoiceSetMuteFlag` (import gwUynkEgNFY,
         PLT 0x12ABC50). Two of its three callers (0xB49210, 0xB49290) search a 4-entry voice-port
         table for a port id and, on a miss, call it with rdi = 0. shadPS4 stubs libSceVoice, so no
         port is ever registered and the miss is certain: the client faulted here in 'cleanup'
         after character:prologue (run 20261013-125227-later-56578-sendmsg-fix, host fault at
         eboot+0xB47E50). Replaced with `xor eax,eax; ret` - the 0 shadPS4's stub would return -
         without the dereference. Original bytes 8B 7F 08. -->
    <PatchList>
      <Line Type="bytes" Address="F47E50" Value="31C0C3"/>
      <!-- The rest of the voice-port wrapper layer, same treatment (2026-10-13, after a second
           cleanup fault at eboot+0xB47CA8 in run 20261013-125554-later-56578-lab-orbit):
           0xB47C40 SetMuteFlag, 0xB47C50 ConnectIPortToOPort, 0xB47C60 DisconnectIPortFromOPort,
           0xB47CA8 GetPortInfo (after its own `mov qword [rsi+8],0`), 0xB47F00 the ResetPort pair
           wrapper. Each dereferenced a port object that cannot exist under stubbed libSceVoice;
           each now returns 0, which is what shadPS4's stub returns. Original bytes 8B 3F (x4),
           55 48 89. The CreatePort thunks write into their own object and are left alone. -->
      <Line Type="bytes" Address="F47C40" Value="31C0C3"/>
      <Line Type="bytes" Address="F47C50" Value="31C0C3"/>
      <Line Type="bytes" Address="F47C60" Value="31C0C3"/>
      <Line Type="bytes" Address="F47CA8" Value="31C0C3"/>
      <Line Type="bytes" Address="F47F00" Value="31C0C3"/>
      <!-- Root of the voice faults: the voice manager's "started" byte is set unconditionally at
           0xB483EC (`mov byte [r14],1`) after sceVoiceInit/GetResourceInfo/Start, whatever the
           stubs returned. Every voice entry point (0xB48F80, 0xB49210, 0xB49290, 0xB49310 ...)
           begins `cmp byte [rdi],0; je <return false>`. Writing 0 leaves voice "not started", so
           the whole subsystem takes its own early-outs, as it would on a console without voice.
           Third fault this closes: #DE at 0xB493D9, a divide by a GetPortInfo field the stub never
           fills (run 20261013-125837-later-56578-lab-orbit-b). Original bytes 41 C6 06 01. The
           thunk guards above are kept as a backstop. -->
      <Line Type="bytes" Address="F483EC" Value="41C60600"/>
    </PatchList>
  </Metadata>
  <Metadata Name="D1 56578 lab probe: inactivity timeout 2 minutes (synthetic)"
            isEnabled="true" AppVer="01.00" AppElf="eboot.bin" Author="d1reimagined" PatchVer="1.0">
    <!-- Probe for the idle return to orbit. The client config's defaults constructor (0x34E620)
         stores five timeouts at 0x352583..0x3525AB: +0x3214 = 900000 ms (15 min), +0x3218 and
         +0x321C = 300000 (5 min), +0x3220 = 3600000 (60 min), +0x3224 = 3900000 (65 min). They are
         named tunables (registered at 0x9C2370 with getters 0x10C7750 / 0x10C7850 / 0x10C7950), and
         0x9BE3D0 hands them out by kind. The Tower's idle return comes after 15 minutes, so +0x3214
         is the candidate: this sets its default to 120000 ms (C0 D4 01 00; original A0 BB 0D 00, the
         imm32 of `mov dword [rbx+0x3214], 0xDBBA0` at 0x352583). Expect the return after 2 minutes
         without input if it is the one. -->
    <PatchList>
      <Line Type="bytes" Address="752589" Value="C0D40100"/>
    </PatchList>
  </Metadata>
</Patch>
